Subject: Transport Wii32 RLG records beneath the complete original loader
Upstream-base: f1e9646a7da6950143e77b1daed33a92c931a638

Decode raw model12/stream8/packet48 bytes into the actual native declared
records. Retain all source scalar/unknown words and encoded offsets/hash IDs.
Grow only original GLM_Header record allocation footprints, retaining the
original calls, resource pool, label order and per-method remainder copying.
Map raw stream-table byte offsets to actual native record width and use
native pointer carriers beneath unchanged source Fixup loops. Guard the
existing native matrix pointer cast so the whole console source is pristine.

This is permanent serialized/native ABI adaptation, not an unfinished-source
workaround or behavior fix. Entire Read/traversal/registration/finalization
decisions remain original. Full raw chunk/parameter/index/matrix endian and
suballocation/frame/pop ownership still need qualification before actual
Read, array registration or rendering. No readiness or alternate loader.

